UNKNOWN OPERATOR

  × Nash does not use (%) as the remainder operator:
   ╭─[Main.nash:1:1]
 1 │ name = other
   · ────
   ╰────
  help: If you want the behavior of (%) like in JavaScript, use the integer remainder
        function. If you want modular arithmetic like in math, use the integer modulus
        function. The difference is how things work when negative numbers are involved.
